// Test: bugfixes/list_join_requires_string_list
// Grammar: namespace_function_call
// Semantic: SEM001 — list.join(items, sep) is the same operation as
//   string.join and takes a list<string> (stdlib-reference.md §5)
// Fixed in: compiler 0.33.190
// Expected output:
// Expected error:
//   cannot be used as
//
// Regression: list.join on list<integer> compiled and returned ",," because
// every element was read as a string pointer.

start:
	list<integer> nums = [1, 2, 3]
	print("[" + list.join(nums, ",") + "]")
